1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,183
One patient. Eight letters.

2
00:00:02,302 --> 00:00:07,650
An anaesthetist, a surgeon and an
emergency doctor each need different facts.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,773
Letters copy each other, so errors travel.

4
00:00:11,893 --> 00:00:17,675
One duplex report says the right
carotid; every other letter says left.

5
00:00:17,795 --> 00:00:21,650
A twelve kilo weight loss
is mentioned nowhere.

6
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,303
Second Eye starts from one sentence.

7
00:00:25,423 --> 00:00:33,650
The anaesthetist types her task, and the app
works out the role and what that task needs.

8
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:40,266
One screen, only what matters: blood
thinner, allergy, heart function,

9
00:00:40,386 --> 00:00:43,318
and what is not documented.

10
00:00:43,438 --> 00:00:51,650
Click any fact and the original German sentence
lights up, with an English translation.

11
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:55,580
Switch the doctor, keep the patient.

12
00:00:55,700 --> 00:01:03,650
The surgeon and the emergency physician each
get a different screen, built for their task.

13
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:07,080
The record disagrees with itself.

14
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:13,633
Second Eye found five contradictions
and shows both passages side by side.

15
00:01:13,753 --> 00:01:19,650
It also lists blind spots and
follow-ups that were never closed.

16
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:23,558
How it works: AI points, code verifies.

17
00:01:23,678 --> 00:01:29,093
Every quote is checked against the
letters, so nothing is made up.

18
00:01:29,213 --> 00:01:31,469
Rules handle what rules can.

19
00:01:31,589 --> 00:01:35,650
Built on IBM's MLA output
and the IPS structure.

20
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:42,527
On the five test situations: fifteen of fifteen
answers, every fact linked, zero invented.

21
00:01:42,647 --> 00:01:49,650
Not yet: the PIN lock isn't wired in, and
guideline citations still need a second reviewer.

22
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:52,628
Other tools summarise the record.

23
00:01:52,748 --> 00:01:57,650
Second Eye checks it, for
the task in front of you.
